<<
/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261106120346\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics PDF pipeline)
/Keywords (polycrisis resilience\054 systemic risk\054 vulnerability reduction\054 preventive capacity\054 transformative capacity\054 interconnected crises\054 development as resilience\054 sustainable development\054 convergence\054 multi\055dividend interventions\054 development policy\054 disaster mortality)
/ModDate (D\07220261106120346\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (The defining risks of this century do not arrive one at a time\056 Climate change\054 environmental degradation\054 economic instability\054 geopolitical conflict\054 demographic change\054 public health threats\054 technological disruption and fragile infrastructure now act on one another\054 so that the harm entangled crises cause together exceeds the sum of their separate effects\056 This flagship report sets out a concept for that condition\054 Polycrisis Resilience\054 and a framework for building it\054 the H Heuristics Polycrisis Resilience Framework\054 which it presents as concepts developed by Hunter Hughes\054 Founder of H Heuristics\056 It defines Polycrisis Resilience as the capacity of individuals\054 communities\054 institutions\054 economies\054 societies and interconnected systems to anticipate\054 withstand\054 adapt to\054 recover from and reduce their vulnerability to multiple interacting crises\056)
/Title (Polycrisis Resilience\072 A General Definition and the H Heuristics Framework\072 The Capacity to Anticipate\054 Withstand\054 Adapt to\054 Recover from and Reduce Vulnerability to Multiple Interacting Crises)
/Trapped /False
>>
